.TH STOP\-MU2EDAQ\-CONTROLCENTER.SH 1 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-controlcenter 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh \- stop the Mu2e DAQ Control Center kiosk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh
.PP
.B stop.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardized Mu2e control-room stop script for
.BR controlcenter (1).
It resolves the running process, sends
.BR SIGTERM ,
waits up to 10 seconds for a clean exit, escalates to
.B SIGKILL
if the process is still alive, and removes the PID file.
.PP
.B stop.sh
is a symbolic link to this script;
.B stop-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh
is the canonical name, for the same collision reason described in
.BR start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh (1).
.SS PID resolution
The PID is read from
.I controlcenter.pid
when that file exists.  When it does not, the script falls back to
.B "pgrep -f controlcenter.py"
and takes the first match.
.PP
The fallback matches on the script name only, so a second Control
Center started from a different checkout, or an editor holding
.I controlcenter.py
in its command line, can be selected instead of the intended process.
Prefer keeping the PID file intact.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  The script parses no arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I controlcenter.pid
Written by
.BR start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh (1);
removed on every exit path that resolves a PID.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
None.  Unlike the start script this one does not consult
.BR CRS_PORT_CMD ;
it acts on the process, not the port.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The process was stopped, was already gone, or was not running.  This
script does not report a non-zero status for an already-stopped
application, which is what makes it safe to run from a desktop icon.
.SH EXAMPLES
Stop a locally started instance:
.PP
.nf
  ./stop-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh
.fi
.PP
Stop it through the control-room wrapper:
.PP
.nf
  crs-app stop controlcenter
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR controlcenter (1),
.BR start-mu2edaq-controlcenter.sh (1),
.BR crs-app (1),
.BR mu2edaq-app (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group.
